(D4 - Discrepancy 4 repro, RESOLVED by vox #277. The field is written
 `a text called label is "post"`, a text field with a text default. Up to
 vox 0.4.15 a thing could not hold a text field, and the program was
 refused twice: first "Field 'label' of thing 'stamp' is a text, but its
 default is a text", naming the same type twice, then "... is a text,
 which a thing cannot hold yet".
 A thing can now hold a text field (LANGUAGE.md:993-994): the default
 works, a copy never shares its text with the original (LANGUAGE.md:
 995-997), and a text field compares by its characters (LANGUAGE.md:
 1401-1402). Re-recorded 2026-10-13 on vox main a0a2ecc.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D4.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   {label: "post"}
   {label: "post"}
   {label: "other"}
   differ
)
A thing called stamp has
  a text called label is "post".

a stamp called s.
Print s.
a stamp called t is s.
Set t's label to "other".
Print s.
Print t.
If s is t then, Print "same".
Otherwise, Print "differ".
